WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.200
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.490
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:06.080
between breakfast cereals
in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.323
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.280
Hey, everyone, Joe from "Food Wars."

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.580
I'm actually not in this episode,

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.050
because myself, Conner, and Yuelei

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.310
are busy making a new
season of "Food Wars"

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.950
with a new country.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.810
Ooh!

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.080
But don't worry, I'll chime
in every once in a while

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.520
and be super annoying.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.720
We're doing a cereal episode.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.370
Now, obviously there are
a lot of breakfast cereals

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.390
in the UK and the US,

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.180
and we can't cover them
all in one episode.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.147
So we're going to start with the two

00:00:28.147 --> 00:00:29.613
best sellers in America,

00:00:29.613 --> 00:00:32.150
which are Frosted Flakes
and Honey Nut Cheerios.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.900
Then, after that, we might
get into some fun cereals

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.020
which you can't find in
one country or the other.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.410
That sound good to you, Irene?

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.843
Yeah, sounds great, Harry.

00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:43.700
First things first, Frosted Flakes?

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.668
What is going on there?

00:00:44.668 --> 00:00:47.110
In the UK, we actually
just call them Frosties.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.690
OK, this is the one time I think the UK

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.280
has a better term for something.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.810
'Cause Frosties is actually kind of cute.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.120
It's like besties.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.830
In the UK, Frosties come in five sizes,

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.951
starting with this one,
which is a 25-gram box,

00:00:59.951 --> 00:01:02.370
which comes as part of
one of these multipacks.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.800
From there, we move up to a 375-gram box.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.050
Next up, we've got a
500-gram box of Frosties.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:12.380
From there, we move up to a 750-gram box.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.569
Then our largest size is this one,

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:16.900
the big 1-kilogram box.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.800
In the US, Frosted Flakes
also come in four sizes.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.690
We start with the 60-gram cup,

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.240
which you can just add
milk directly into and eat.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.430
Next up, we have the 24-ounce,

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:30.780
or 680-gram, family-size box.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.430
From there, we move up
to a 34-ounce mega size,

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.360
but this actually isn't the largest one.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.460
We actually go one step further, with a

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.868
[bag crunching]

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:47.860
39.5-ounce, or 1,120-gram, bag.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:53.645
That means our largest size
is 12% larger than the UK's.

00:01:53.645 --> 00:01:55.860
In the UK, the recommended
serving size for Frosties

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.020
is 30 grams,

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.278
which means that our largest box

00:01:58.278 --> 00:02:00.586
contains roughly 33 servings.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.080
Let's find out what 30 grams of Frosties

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.170
actually looks like.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.270
Digital scales! We finally
got digital scales.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.612
I leave for one episode
and we get the digi scales.

00:02:07.612 --> 00:02:09.346
What the heck, guys? I want one.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.372
How precise can we go?

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.210
[laughs] Not very.

00:02:17.442 --> 00:02:21.283
That is 30.08 grams of
Frosties right there.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:26.007
In an actual cereal bowl, that is nothing.

00:02:26.007 --> 00:02:30.060
In the US, the recommended
serving size for Frosted Flakes

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.810
is actually 37 grams,

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.620
which is 23% more than in the UK.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.490
So while our largest packet
size might be a little bigger,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.390
we're technically getting fewer servings.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.591
Just 30 compared to the UK's 33.

00:02:43.591 --> 00:02:45.621
[bag crackles]

00:02:45.621 --> 00:02:50.621
Does this count as ASMR? [bag crunching]

00:02:56.134 --> 00:02:57.990
37. I did it.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:58.980
I feel like -- you know on Tinder

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.730
when guys hold, like,
a fish in their photo?

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.703
I feel like that right now.

00:03:02.703 --> 00:03:03.900
Now, I'm going to be honest here,

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.870
that is not a realistic serving size

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.320
for a strapping young lad such as myself.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.320
What I'm going to do is pour out

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.900
what I would consider to be a normal bowl,

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.030
and then we'll weigh that
to see what it comes to.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.893
So, my actual realistic
serving ended up being

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:16.851
almost exactly double the 30 grams,

00:03:16.851 --> 00:03:18.251
coming in at around 60 grams.

00:03:19.223 --> 00:03:22.370
57.5. OK, this is 60.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.330
If I was using a bowl,

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.260
I think this is exactly what
I would pour for myself.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.500
'Cause I feel like what people do,

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.010
you fill the entire bowl of cereal,

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.440
and then you fill it up with milk.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.460
But the thing I, for some reason, do,

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.870
is I eat my cereal out
of a cup. Like, a mug.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.961
I like that it's deeper.

00:03:36.961 --> 00:03:38.619
So I'll put that in,

00:03:38.619 --> 00:03:41.800
and so I don't know what the
equivalent of that would be.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.020
But, yeah, cereal out of a mug.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.190
It's, like, it's fun.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.280
The first thing to point out here

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.590
is that I really gaslit myself

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:51.450
and was convinced that we had
Honey Nut Cheerios in the UK.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.530
However, when I then looked into it,

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.903
I found that instead,
they're just Honey Cheerios

00:03:54.903 --> 00:03:56.920
and I'd imagined the whole thing.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.475
Although our cameraman, Charlie,

00:03:58.475 --> 00:04:00.210
today was convinced of the same thing,

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.980
so maybe there's just
some butterfly effect

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.388
that's going on.

00:04:03.388 --> 00:04:05.840
Honey Cheerios in the UK
come in six portion sizes,

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.060
starting with this one.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.530
It's a 30-gram box.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:12.000
And, again, it only comes
as part of a multipack.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.110
From there, we go up to a 280-gram box.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.560
While I was looking for the portions,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.635
I found both a 370-gram box

00:04:19.635 --> 00:04:22.460
as well as this 375-gram box.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.670
It looks like this one,

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.800
maybe they are trying
to use less packaging

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.930
but have taken that
opportunity to give you

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.848
a few less Cheerios as well.

00:04:30.848 --> 00:04:31.681
Who knows?

00:04:31.681 --> 00:04:33.050
Our next size is this one,

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.995
which is a 515-gram box.

00:04:35.995 --> 00:04:39.370
And then, finally, our largest
Cheerios box is this one,

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:42.220
which is 575 grams.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:45.260
Honey Nut Cheerios in the
US come in five sizes.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.026
We have the 1.8-ounce,

00:04:48.026 --> 00:04:50.362
or 51-gram, mini cup.

00:04:50.362 --> 00:04:53.375
The classic 10.8-ounce box.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.443
The 18.8-ounce family size.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.011
The 29.4-ounce mega size.

00:05:03.011 --> 00:05:05.510
[bag crunching]

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.140
And, lastly, a 32-ounce,

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.400
or 907-gram, bag.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.320
That makes the largest US option

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.401
57% larger than the UK's.

00:05:15.401 --> 00:05:16.894
The recommended serving size for Cheerios

00:05:16.894 --> 00:05:18.977
in the UK is, again, 30 grams.

00:05:18.977 --> 00:05:22.270
That means that our largest box
contains around 19 servings.

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:25.160
In the US, the recommended
serving size is 1 cup.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.530
See, that's why you should
eat it out of a cup. Get it?

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.750
Which should weigh around 37 grams.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:32.480
That's a 23% increase on the UK.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.020
And the most servings you
can get in a US container

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.310
would be around 24.5,

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.210
which is almost a 30% increase on the UK,

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.690
because of course.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.570
But once again, it seems like 30 grams

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.430
is just a really unrealistic serving size.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:47.870
I think, again, I'm eating
much closer to 60 grams.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.215
Does that look about right to you, Irene?

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:50.870
[cereal clinking]

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.328
Yeah. I agree with Harry.

00:05:52.328 --> 00:05:54.620
This is, again, it's --
you need to fill the bowl.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.378
So apparently filling the
bowl means 60 grams, so.

00:05:57.378 --> 00:06:00.000
No one's pouring out 37 grams of Cheerios.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.448
This is, I think this is how much

00:06:01.448 --> 00:06:03.160
normal people are pouring out.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.710
So realistically, you're
only actually getting

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.180
nine and a half servings
out of the UK's largest box.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:10.933
Whereas we're getting 15
servings from our largest bag.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.905
Wow, you guys are getting
kind of ripped off.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.623
Unfortunately, we don't
have any exclusive Frosties

00:06:18.623 --> 00:06:19.613
in the UK.

00:06:19.613 --> 00:06:21.770
Here are all the Frosted
Flakes from the US

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.750
that you won't find in the UK.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.280
We have the chocolate Frosted Flakes,

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.370
Frosted Flakes with marshmallows,

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.930
Frosted Flakes Cinnamon Basketballs,

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.560
honey nut Frosted Flakes,

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.810
Frosted Flakes and Froot Loops mash-up.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.060
This is limited edition.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.895
And the Tiger Paws Jumbo Snax.

00:06:38.895 --> 00:06:41.423
Eh, I'll try one of the basketballs.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.362
Tastes like cinnamon.

00:06:44.362 --> 00:06:45.553
I don't think it's that good.

00:06:45.553 --> 00:06:49.340
Shaq will put his face
on literally anything.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.510
Look at that smile he has
on that face right there.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.110
That's that, "I'm getting paid! Whoo!"

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.680
He's hanging out with
Tony the Tiger. Right?

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.570
He also does a commercial
with the General.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.000
"Space Jam" should have been that.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.865
It should have been Shaq with
all the cartoon characters

00:07:02.865 --> 00:07:04.300
of products that he advertises with.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.935
It'd be Shaq, the General, Tony the Tiger,

00:07:07.935 --> 00:07:09.410
a can of Arizona iced tea.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.470
What else is he doing?

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:12.530
That would have been a much better movie.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:13.560
This, this is exciting.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.050
This is a fake novelty.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.200
This is a real novelty.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.070
These are literally like Lucky Charms.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.532
I'm only eating the marshmallows.

00:07:19.532 --> 00:07:21.640
And you know it would turn the
milk, like, purple or pink,

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:22.973
or, like, a weird, ugly color,

00:07:22.973 --> 00:07:25.140
but it would taste so good.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:27.670
I'm sorry you can't have this, Harry.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.779
You know what? It's
probably banned in the UK

00:07:29.779 --> 00:07:30.800
because of the hormones

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.067
or, like, artificial products anyway.

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:35.239
These are interesting.

00:07:35.239 --> 00:07:37.050
Oh, my God! OK.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.280
This looks like the baby cereal.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.300
Like the baby snacks or
like the toddler snacks.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.240
They are! It looks like the baby cereal.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.973
It's like --

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.460
but it's a little bit bigger.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:47.643
Very exciting.

00:07:47.643 --> 00:07:49.151
[crunching]

00:07:49.151 --> 00:07:51.070
It's not dry. It's not as sweet.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.460
I would add more sugar to this. [laughs]

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:54.943
I have, like, my dipping sugar.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:00.070
Unfortunately, we don't have
any exclusive Cheerio options

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:01.210
in the UK.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.570
Here are all the Cheerios
you'll find in the US

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.310
but not in the UK.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.565
Here we have the more fruity flavors.

00:08:07.565 --> 00:08:10.880
Blueberry Cheerios,
apple cinnamon Cheerios,

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.243
multigrain Cheerios with strawberries,

00:08:13.243 --> 00:08:14.850
Very Berry Cheerios,

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.610
chocolate strawberry Cheerios,

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.720
and fruity Cheerios.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.860
Is this supposed to be like
their take on Froot Loops?

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.345
Like healthy Froot Loops?

00:08:25.261 --> 00:08:26.600
No.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:29.580
We have pumpkin spice Cheerios,

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.540
Honey Nut Cheerios medley,

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:33.687
cinnamon Cheerios,

00:08:33.687 --> 00:08:35.620
maple Cheerios,

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:37.460
frosted Cheerios,

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.750
chocolate peanut butter Cheerios,

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.421
Cheerios Oat Crunch oats and honey,

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:45.100
and Cheerios Oat Crunch almond.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.567
We weren't able to get our hands

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:48.570
on the limited-edition flavors

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:51.780
toasted coconut, peach, and banana nut.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.100
I'm a big pumpkin spice girl.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.123
I think it's good.

00:08:55.303 --> 00:08:57.578
Mm, smells like fall.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.340
Honestly, I don't even
know if it was that good

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.390
or I'm just like, it's pumpkin spice,

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:06.097
so I'm just automatically thinking

00:09:06.097 --> 00:09:08.550
it smells and tastes good.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.075
But I think this would be amazing.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.950
Here are some British cereals

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.580
which you won't find in the US.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.500
Here are some cereals
you won't find in the UK.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:22.290
Let's start with a US
classic, Lucky Charms.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.080
I do think they are a classic,

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.530
and the marshmallows are really good.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:26.840
They do taste very artificial,

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.104
but they're supposed to taste artificial.

00:09:29.104 --> 00:09:30.380
And I stand by that.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.690
I've never had Lucky Charms before.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.258
I had to go to one of those American shops

00:09:33.258 --> 00:09:35.118
on Oxford Street to get one.

00:09:35.118 --> 00:09:37.685
So are those all marshmallows,
all those colorful things?

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.820
It tastes like a marshmallow,
but it's, like, crunchy?

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:44.996
Marshmallows aren't
supposed to be crispy, guys.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.823
I'd be lying if I said those weren't good.

00:09:49.823 --> 00:09:50.820
That is good.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.710
Everything about the design
of this is just to, like,

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.010
make a child go, "Oh,
my God, I need this."

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:58.140
Yes, American cereal boxes
look like slot machines.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.250
That is by design.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:03.160
So, next up we've got Froot Loops.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.882
I think Froot Loops is one of
those cereals you can eat dry,

00:10:05.882 --> 00:10:07.450
because they have enough flavor to them.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:09.969
Now look, the colors are so fun.

00:10:09.969 --> 00:10:11.171
Look how fun that is.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:15.380
Something's wrong with this one.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.159
They didn't used to taste like this.

00:10:17.159 --> 00:10:19.940
[gasps] They used to
use artificial red dye,

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:22.600
and they switched to a natural one.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.110
They went too natural.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.600
Also never tried these.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.655
I like the toucan guy. He's cool.

00:10:30.052 --> 00:10:32.602
Whoo! Jesus Christ! [laughs]

00:10:32.602 --> 00:10:34.260
The smell of those!

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:38.440
Whoo-hooh! What is that?

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.989
Charlie: Smells like
soap, or like shower gel.

00:10:40.989 --> 00:10:42.305
Yeah.

00:10:42.305 --> 00:10:44.610
Like a tropical shampoo.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.803
Charlie: Like a cheap bodywash.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:50.510
No, I don't like that.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:52.980
The same acidic smell that I got,

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.550
you can taste that as well.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.110
And that is not something
that you want with milk.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:00.660
And, finally, Cap'n Crunch.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.210
I think the other

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:05.057
traditional sugary cereals
are just superior to it.

00:11:05.057 --> 00:11:06.574
This is just so, like,

00:11:06.574 --> 00:11:08.540
it doesn't offer anything, you know?

00:11:09.466 --> 00:11:10.299
Ugh.

00:11:10.299 --> 00:11:11.684
You can see where all the Yellow 5

00:11:11.684 --> 00:11:13.097
and Yellow 6 are going.

00:11:14.339 --> 00:11:16.900
[crunching]

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.093
They are crunchy, as the name suggests.

00:11:19.093 --> 00:11:19.926
They're pretty good.

00:11:19.926 --> 00:11:20.910
It's between these or Lucky Charms.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.600
Froot Loops for me are awful.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.590
Never -- stop eating those.

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:25.940
We'll start with a
personal favorite of mine,

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:26.900
which is Golden Nuggets.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.080
I'm a little surprised you
don't have these in the US,

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.068
because the kind of advert campaign

00:11:31.068 --> 00:11:33.270
was based around prospecting
and the gold rush.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:36.223
So we've got a little
mascot gold miner guy,

00:11:36.223 --> 00:11:37.160
who I think his name was, like,

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.964
Prospector Pete or something like that.

00:11:38.964 --> 00:11:42.030
I do feel like they used to
be brighter than that. Yeah.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.330
But they've got rid of the
catchphrase and also, yeah,

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.540
demoted the mascot to
the back of the pack.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.420
The catchphrase when I
remember growing up with these

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:53.200
was, "They taste yeehaw!"

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.470
OK, "They taste yeehaw."

00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:58.157
What would be the UK
equivalent of that in America?

00:11:58.157 --> 00:12:00.240
British Parliament Flakes.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.290
What'd you just say?

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:06.063
Parliament Pops. They taste jolly good.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.070
I don't think they taste quite as yeehaw

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:11.270
as I remember from my childhood,

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:13.600
but it's still, like, a solid

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:15.390
mid to low level of yeehaw.

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:16.440
Next up, we've got Weetabix.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:17.900
Now, I personally love Weetabix,

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.316
but I will say it's quite a boring cereal.

00:12:20.316 --> 00:12:22.587
If you imagine the kind of archetypal,

00:12:22.587 --> 00:12:25.190
really boring, gray British breakfast,

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.510
it's probably one of these.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:29.831
It's literally just compressed wheat

00:12:29.831 --> 00:12:31.679
with a very small amount of sugar

00:12:31.679 --> 00:12:34.680
and I think some enriched
vitamins and minerals.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:36.760
Like, they have no right
to be as good as they are,

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:37.750
but they are just good.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.240
Like, I can't explain why.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:41.379
As long as the milk is really cold,

00:12:41.379 --> 00:12:44.423
so that you get the
crisp that's maintained.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:50.551
To me, that's just pure nostalgia.

00:12:50.551 --> 00:12:53.326
So, we got

00:12:53.326 --> 00:12:54.976
Harry's

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:58.220
British cereal.

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:59.713
I'm very confused by this.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:01.736
Scared.

00:13:01.736 --> 00:13:03.628
I'm going to follow Harry's tutorial.

00:13:05.576 --> 00:13:06.409
OK.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.430
I don't think you can
just call something cereal

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.760
because you're pouring milk on top of it.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:14.330
And I feel like that's
what's happening here.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:15.513
Like, this kind of feels like

00:13:15.513 --> 00:13:17.500
if I were to get a granola bar

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.783
and pour milk on top of it

00:13:18.783 --> 00:13:19.758
and I was going to be like,

00:13:19.758 --> 00:13:21.367
"Oh, I'm eating cereal now."

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.650
I don't want to say it
tastes like cardboard,

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.600
but it tastes like cardboard.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.347
My childhood was Fruity
Pebbles. I'm sorry.

00:13:29.347 --> 00:13:32.690
It was rainbows and unicorns
and magical flavors.

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:34.106
If you did want a slightly more exciting

00:13:34.106 --> 00:13:34.980
version of Weetabix,

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.310
then they do have flavored ones as well.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:38.100
For example, these are
the classic biscuits

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.403
but banana flavored.

00:13:39.403 --> 00:13:42.390
There are also some classic
ones but chocolate flavored.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:43.760
Then they have a few
other options as well,

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.503
such as these ones, which
are chocolate melts.

00:13:47.503 --> 00:13:49.510
So it's kind of like a
Weetabix outside layer,

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.195
but then with a little
bit of chocolate inside.

00:13:51.195 --> 00:13:52.945
And these come with milk chocolate

00:13:52.945 --> 00:13:54.350
or with white chocolate.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.766
And then, finally, maybe
my favorite cereal ever,

00:13:57.766 --> 00:13:59.110
Weetabix crispy minis.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.660
These things are incredible.

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:03.010
It's little bite-size versions of Weetabix

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:04.490
with a bunch of chocolate chips in them.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:06.250
Honestly, God-tier cereal.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:09.993
This is supposed to be,
like, the treat version.

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:21.310
Food is supposed to make you feel better.

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.480
A final UK exclusive for today are Weetos.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:25.780
Now, not so much of a fan of these myself.

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:27.171
They're kind of like Cheerios

00:14:27.171 --> 00:14:28.760
in that they're a ring shape,

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.320
however they're a little bit bigger,

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.410
a little bit more puffy and airy.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:33.820
And, personally, I just don't love that,

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:35.570
'cause when you're eating
them with the milk,

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.770
they go a little bit
more soggy more quickly.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:40.220
Yeah, I'm sure some people
like them, but not myself.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:47.004
This is a more realistic
serving of 60 grams

00:14:47.004 --> 00:14:48.580
of Frosted Flakes.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:49.840
If we do some quick math,

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.973
we can figure out that
the nutrition for this

00:14:51.973 --> 00:14:53.356
is as follows:

00:14:53.356 --> 00:14:55.339
210 calories;

00:14:55.339 --> 00:14:56.522
0 grams of fat;

00:14:56.522 --> 00:14:58.580
53.4 grams of carbs,

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.966
19.2 grams of which are sugar;

00:15:00.966 --> 00:15:03.074
1.62 grams of fiber;

00:15:03.074 --> 00:15:06.535
and 307 milligrams of sodium.

00:15:06.535 --> 00:15:07.470
So, here's everything that's in

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:09.660
60 grams of Frosties in the UK:

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:11.000
225 calories;

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:12.550
0.36 grams of fat,

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.275
of which 0.06 grams are saturated;

00:15:15.275 --> 00:15:17.300
carbs, 52.2 grams,

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:19.707
of which 22.2 grams are sugar;

00:15:19.707 --> 00:15:21.465
fiber, 1.4 grams;

00:15:21.465 --> 00:15:23.881
and 232 milligrams of sodium.

00:15:23.881 --> 00:15:24.920
The final thing to note

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:26.780
is that these values don't include milk.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:27.613
So, in the States,

00:15:27.613 --> 00:15:29.150
we have a few different types of milk

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.623
with varying fat content.

00:15:30.623 --> 00:15:33.423
Skim milk, which has 0% fat;

00:15:33.423 --> 00:15:35.423
1% milk; 2% milk;

00:15:35.423 --> 00:15:39.650
and then whole milk,
which is around 3.25% fat.

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:42.600
For this example, we're
going to use 2% milk.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.930
In the UK, we don't refer to
our milks by fat percentage.

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.124
Instead, we call them
skimmed, semi-skimmed,

00:15:47.124 --> 00:15:48.030
and whole milk.

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:51.850
They're around 0%, 2%, and
3.5% fat, respectively.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:55.186
For this example, we'll
use semi-skimmed milk.

00:15:55.186 --> 00:15:57.840
So, in the UK, we also standardize
the colors of our milk.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.920
So green is always semi-skimmed,

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.278
blue is always whole milk,

00:16:01.278 --> 00:16:02.578
and red is skimmed milk.

00:16:02.578 --> 00:16:04.160
Whereas I spoke to a few American friends,

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:05.770
and those are just,
like, all over the place

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:06.880
depending on where in the country you are.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:08.680
And it seems like an absolute minefield.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:11.780
So, in the US, 100 milliliters of 2% milk

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.540
contains the following:

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:14.665
50 calories;

00:16:14.665 --> 00:16:16.715
2.08 grams of total fat,

00:16:16.715 --> 00:16:19.180
1.25 grams of which are saturated;

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:20.488
5 grams of carbs,

00:16:20.488 --> 00:16:21.640
of which 5 grams are sugar,

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:23.715
so all the carbs are sugar;

00:16:23.715 --> 00:16:26.773
and 52 milligrams of sodium.

00:16:26.773 --> 00:16:29.090
In the UK, 100 milliliters
of semi-skimmed milk

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.190
contains the following:

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:31.140
50 calories;

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:32.265
1.8 grams of fat,

00:16:32.265 --> 00:16:34.274
of which 1.1 grams are saturated;

00:16:34.274 --> 00:16:35.366
4.8 grams of carbs,

00:16:35.366 --> 00:16:37.365
of which 4.8 grams are sugar;

00:16:37.365 --> 00:16:38.690
and 40 milligrams of sodium.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.260
Our research suggests that
the average bowl of cereal

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:43.830
contains around 200 milliliters of milk.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:47.080
So these figures need to be doubled.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:48.160
Harry: Then we can add those stats to our

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.487
realistic 60-gram serving,

00:16:49.487 --> 00:16:52.100
and our final tally looks
something like this.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:55.830
So, the same bowl in the
US would contain this.

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:57.740
So the UK version is
actually more calorific

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:59.012
and more sugary.

00:16:59.012 --> 00:17:02.940
While the US version has more
fat, total carbs, and sodium.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:04.350
Because of course we do.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:05.410
The main thing to watch out for here

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.690
is, of course, the sugar.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.850
The recommended daily added
sugar intake for an adult

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:12.420
is 50 grams, and this
contains over 60% of that.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.537
We're going to measure it out for you now,

00:17:13.537 --> 00:17:16.420
so you can see just how much
sugar is in one of these bowls.

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:20.868
Oh, my God, stop eating so much sugar!

00:17:20.868 --> 00:17:21.990
I feel like this is bad to say,

00:17:21.990 --> 00:17:23.910
but this isn't as much sugar
as I thought there would be.

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:25.270
I thought there would be more.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.307
And, like, sometimes I add
more sugar to my cereal,

00:17:28.307 --> 00:17:29.140
so, like ...

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:31.660
Cereal is meant to be
sugary! I stand by that.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:32.493
So it's like,

00:17:32.493 --> 00:17:34.784
I don't trust people who
eat, like, Raisin Bran.

00:17:34.784 --> 00:17:36.620
Raisin Bran people can't be trusted.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:40.697
This is probably about as much
sugar I add to my coffee, so.

00:17:41.627 --> 00:17:42.460
Look at --

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.968
OK, this is a little bit
more sugar than I would do.

00:17:44.968 --> 00:17:47.190
My stomach hurts just watching this.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.390
This is genuinely good to me.

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:51.170
The 31.8 grams of sugar
in this bowl of Frosties

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.220
is actually less than

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:54.870
three American glazed ring
Krispy Kreme doughnuts.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:55.860
So,

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:57.850
yeah, I guess you can just eat
those for breakfast instead.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:17:58.860
Here's the nutritional info

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:01.500
for a 60-gram bowl of
Honey Cheerios in the UK.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.510
And here are the values

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:05.600
for a 60-gram Honey Nut
Cheerio bowl in the US.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.517
Here's how the values
change if we add milk.

00:18:08.517 --> 00:18:10.230
So this bowl only contains around

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.360
16% of your daily calories,

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.760
but once again,

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.730
it's the sugar you need to watch out for.

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:19.450
There's almost 60% of your
daily sugar allowance in here.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.770
It's not quite as bad in the UK,

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.760
at just 46% of your daily sugar.

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:24.610
But that is still quite
a lot for your breakfast.

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:26.140
But good news for the UK
is that we somehow have

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:28.732
45% less sodium than the US bowl.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:34.264
Here are all the ingredients
in Frosties in the UK.

00:18:34.264 --> 00:18:37.753
Maize, sugar, barley
malt flavouring, salt,

00:18:37.753 --> 00:18:38.730
vitamins and minerals:

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.369
niacin, iron,

00:18:40.369 --> 00:18:43.414
B6, B2, B1, folic acid,

00:18:43.414 --> 00:18:45.636
vitamin D, and vitamin B12.

00:18:45.636 --> 00:18:49.110
Yes, we pronounce it
vih-tamins, not vye-tamins.

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:52.350
Here are all the ingredients
in Frosted Flakes in the US.

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:56.158
Milled corn, sugar, malt flavor, salt,

00:18:56.158 --> 00:18:57.640
vitamins and minerals:

00:18:57.640 --> 00:18:59.854
iron, niacinamide,

00:18:59.854 --> 00:19:02.190
vitamin B6, vitamin B2,

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:04.460
vitamin B1, folic acid,

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:07.080
vitamin D3, and vitamin B12.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.810
The differences here are
actually just linguistic.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:11.340
In practical terms, those are
basically identical lists.

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:12.538
Things get more interesting

00:19:12.538 --> 00:19:15.996
when we move away from
classic Frosted Flakes.

00:19:15.996 --> 00:19:17.288
Take these Frosted Flakes

00:19:17.288 --> 00:19:20.270
with crispy cinnamon
basketballs for example.

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.543
Here's the ingredients list for these.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.450
Two things to watch out for here.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:25.930
Firstly, Yellow 6.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:26.763
This is a food coloring

00:19:26.763 --> 00:19:29.100
which is used to give things
a yellowy-orange color,

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.183
but you're unlikely to see it

00:19:30.183 --> 00:19:31.883
on any ingredients list in the UK.

00:19:31.883 --> 00:19:35.340
It was flagged in a 2008
study as one of six colorings

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:37.660
that may be linked to
hyperactivity in kids.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.420
If it's in a UK food product,

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:41.000
it must come with a warning that

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.311
it "may have an adverse effect on activity

00:19:43.311 --> 00:19:45.515
and attention in children."

00:19:45.515 --> 00:19:47.795
The other ingredient to
watch out for here is BHT,

00:19:47.795 --> 00:19:49.930
or butylated hydroxytoluene.

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:50.880
This is an antioxidant

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:52.730
which is used to keep foods fresh.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:56.260
Outside of food use, some
use it to treat herpes.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:58.131
If that's not enough to put you off,

00:19:58.131 --> 00:20:00.251
there are also some studies
which have suggested

00:20:00.251 --> 00:20:04.870
that BHT causes rats to develop tumors.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.630
Yay.
[children cheering]

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:08.160
There's actually very little evidence

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:09.700
to suggest that it could
do the same to humans,

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.353
but its use is still restricted
in places like Australia,

00:20:12.353 --> 00:20:13.970
and certain companies
such as General Mills

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.680
have voluntarily taken steps to remove it

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:17.080
from all their products.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.510
Here's everything in
Honey Cheerios in the UK.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:23.000
Here's everything in Honey
Nut Cheerios in the US.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.010
These are pretty similar lists

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:25.180
with a few minor differences.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.887
In the UK, we seem to put a bit
more emphasis on the grains,

00:20:27.887 --> 00:20:31.220
with wheat, barley, maize,
and rice all being involved,

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:33.491
compared to just oats in the US.

00:20:33.491 --> 00:20:34.500
While we're doing a cereal episode,

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:35.800
we may as well look at the milk used

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:37.380
in both the UK and the US.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:38.541
You may have seen certain headlines

00:20:38.541 --> 00:20:40.024
suggesting that US milk is actually

00:20:40.024 --> 00:20:41.290
banned in the European Union.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.535
That's not completely correct,

00:20:42.535 --> 00:20:43.850
but there are some differences to note

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.710
which do cause issues with imports.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:48.270
The first issue is due to
something called somatic cells.

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:49.960
These are basically just
the white blood cells

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:51.730
which cows will produce
to fight infections

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:52.860
when they get sick.

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:54.560
If you have a higher somatic
cell count in your milk,

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.986
it's probably a sign that it
came from a less healthy cow.

00:20:56.986 --> 00:20:58.190
The general limit for a healthy cow

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.370
is considered to be around
100,000 cells per milliliter,

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:04.010
with 200,000 getting
towards mastitis territory,

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:05.700
which is when the udders get infected.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.390
For milk to be sold in the European Union,

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:09.350
the somatic cell count
can't be any higher than

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:11.480
400,000 cells per milliliter.

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.190
But in the US, it's almost double that.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:14.584
You guys have an upper threshold of

00:21:14.584 --> 00:21:17.250
750,000 cells per milliliter,

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.158
which means that in general,

00:21:18.158 --> 00:21:19.990
you guys tolerate much
sicker cows than we do

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:21.396
in the UK and the EU.

00:21:22.316 --> 00:21:24.910
[laughing] Not the sicker cows.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:26.521
I feel like every time we do one of these,

00:21:26.521 --> 00:21:28.957
it's basically just the UK being like,

00:21:28.957 --> 00:21:30.730
"So, you guys don't standardize anything

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:32.234
and you don't regulate anything."

00:21:32.234 --> 00:21:33.340
And we're like,

00:21:34.237 --> 00:21:35.440
"Yeah."

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.320
The one chocolate chip in my palate

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:39.370
really makes me feel really happy.

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:42.743
I don't need sugar or flavors or color.

